    "killington": {
      "status": "ok",
      "resort": "Killington",
      "adapter": "powdr",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-14 16:24:12",
      "note": "Hey, Beast family, These are the days we dream of this time of year. Soft snow, sunshine, and endless laps all day long. Wednesday brings a change of scenery with wet weather in the forecast, but we’re still in for a good time. We’re expecting a few scattered showers tonight, which should clear up again tomorrow morning, though it may be foggy, especially at the peak. Temps will be hovering right around 60 degrees again, and there’s a good chance the rain returns later in the afternoon. A little water is going to stop us from having a blast out there, though. Due to the warm weather, surface conditions and our snowpack are changing from day to day, but things are riding wicked good overall. The snow will be nice and springlike during the day tomorrow with areas of wet snow and machine groomed hard pack mixed in. Please note that more areas of thin cover and walking required are popping up as the days roll on, but our grooming team is doing all they can to patch things together in low spots each night. Speaking of our groomers, they'll be heading out tonight smoothing out over 35 trails tonight including Upper Skyelark to Lower Bittersweet, which was my favorite run of the day. They are staying off of Superstar, Lower East Fall and some more of our steeper trail to preserve the snowpack, but there will be plenty of soft cord to shred early on. While the trails in the Canyon area are not getting groomed, a handful will remain open with prime spring conditions and a few fun areas where you'll have to pick your line carefully. The bumps aren't stacked to their fullest at the moment, but ungroomed terrain should be loose and a good challenge. Please note that beginner terrain is limited, with easier terrain remaining available at Ramshead. Check the Lifts & Trails Report for the full list of options. We’ll be spinning 5 lifts, with the Superstar Six, K-1 Gondola, Snowdon Six, and Ramshead Express opening at 9:00 a.m., with the North Ridge Quad joining at 9:30 a.m. . On the kparks front, Timberline continues to shine with close to 40 features, 5 jumps, and a halfpipe. Our Parks Crew recently refreshed features ahead of the Spring Send-Off, so it’s still a great spot to take a few laps. Check the Terrain Parks Report for the full details. While many mountains across the East have wrapped up their seasons, we’re still getting after it with plenty of terrain and more spring skiing and spectacular events ahead. This Saturday, April 18, is our Dazed and Defrosted spring event and Winter Season Passholder Appreciation Party . Put it on your radar and we'll catch you at The Beast. Keep on stacking up those days! This season isn't over yet. -Austin Operating Day: 155 Season passes for 26/27 are now on sale! Lock in the lowest price on Beast 365 or Winter Unlimited passes with lots of perks, plus free skiing & riding for the rest of this spring. And there's more good news for families: Youth & Child pass pricing has been significantly reduced for next season, with over $300 in savings available on Beast 365 access. Lifts Key lifts operate seven days a week from 9:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Monday through Friday, and from 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. on Saturday and Sunday. The Superstar Six will close at 5:00 p.m. on April 18, 25, and May 2nd. Starting on May 3rd, the Superstar Six will be open Fri. - Sun. The North Ridge Quad opens at 9:30 a.m. on weekdays and 8:00 a.m. on weekends. Upcoming lift closure dates: Ramshead Express Quad - Sunday, April 19th Snowdon Six- Sunday, April 19th K-1 Gondola - Sunday, April 19th North Ridge Quad - Sunday, April 19th Skyeship Express Gondola Stage II - Open Friday April 17 - Sunday, April 19th (conditions permitting) Skye Peak Express Quad - Open Friday April 17 - Sunday, April 19th (conditions permitting) The Tubing Park presented by bubly is closed for the season. Uphill Travel Please visit killington.com/uphill for specific uphill route information, including a map of each route: Ramshead base to top of Ramshead Express Quad - Open Ramshead Express Quad to top of Snowdon Mountain - CLOSED Snowshed base to the top of Snowshed Slope - CLOSED Base of Sunrise Village Triple to top of Bear Mountain - CLOSED Killington/Pico Mountain Interconnect - CLOSED Pico Base to the top of Golden Express Quad - CLOSED Pico Base to Pico Summit - CLOSED Pico Summit Glade Route - CLOSED Before heading up the hill, be sure to review our uphill travel policies and grab your Uphill Travel Pass here . All uphill travelers are required to have an Uphill Travel Pass and armband, which can be picked up at any ticket window. Please keep an eye out for grooming equipment and steer clear of mountain ops during non-operating hours. MOUNTAIN SERVICES Parking & Shuttles Parking is available at the K-1, Snowshed, Ramshead, and Vale parking lots. Please respect signage and allow our parking staff to assist you on your trip to the slopes. Shuttle service is available from 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. midweek and 6:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends and holidays. Winter car camping and overnight parking is only available in the lot across from Skyeship Lodge, though please note that the Skyeship Lodge is closed for this season. See details here . Lodge Services All lodges listed here are open daily from 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekdays and 7:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. on weekends/peak dates*. K-1 Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served from 10:30 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. daily. Brew Bar (2nd floor): Open serving handcrafted coffees at 8:30 a.m. on weekdays and at 7:30 a.m. on weekends, with cocktails and beers served starting at 9:00 a.m. K-1 Pub (3rd floor): Open at 10:00 a.m. on Friday - Sunday. Rentals & Killington Sports at K-1: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Demos & Tuning: Available via the K-1 Rental Shop from April 10th through May 3rd. All pass holders—including Beast 365 and Unlimited—will receive 50% off demo rentals. Guest Services: 1st floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 1:00 p.m. on weekdays and until 4:30 p.m. on weekends/peak dates. 2nd floor - Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Superstar Umbrella Bar: Open at 11:00 a.m. from Friday - Sunday offering beer, wine, liquor, and specialty hot cocktails. Ramshead Lodge Breakfast: Served starting at 8:30 a.m. on Fridays and 7:30 a.m. on weekends/peak dates. Lunch: Served daily with grab & go options & soups. The pizza station is open Thursday - Monday, and the full grill menu is available Friday - Sunday. Guest Services: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 12:00 p.m. on Monday – Thursday and until 4:30 p.m. on Friday - Sunday at the ticket windows outside of the lodge. Rentals: Open 30 minutes before lifts until 30 minutes after lifts. Child Care Center: Open Monday to Friday from 8:30 a.m. - 3:45 p.m. Closing Date: April 19th Bear Mountain Lodge - Closed for the season. Will re-open for basic lodge services on April 17th - 19th, conditions permitting. Snowshed Lodge - Closed for the season. Snowshed Demos & Tuning remains open seven days a week, providing tuning services for guests and Season Tune holders. Demos also available with more options at K-1. Skyeship Lodge - Closed for the season. On-Mountain Dining Options : Peak Lodge – Closed for the season. Jerk Jamaican Mountain Grill – Closed for the season. Ledgewood Yurt – Closed for the season. Mountain services are subject to change. Please check here daily before making your lunch and lodge choices. Winter Lift Tickets and rentals must be purchased online at this link . Check to see if your pass is good to go using our Online Pass Checker . Find our Season Pass FAQs by clicking here . Season passes for summer 2026 and winter 26/27 are now on sale! Buy now . Have a ticketing question? Our text number ( 802-523-2202 ) is the best way to get it answered quickly, but please note that we cannot process transactions via text. Have a season pass question? Call 1-800-621-MTNS or email seasonpass@killington.com Please visit Killington.com/cancellation for more details on our cancellation policy. Killington Sports at Route 4 is open daily from 10:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Closing date: Sunday, April 19th Killington is a cashless resort. We accept all major credit cards as well as Apple, Google, and Samsung Pay. *No remaining Peak Dates during winter 2025/26. We strive to have the most up-to-date and accurate snow report, but errors can happen from time to time. If you have feedback or a correction for us, please share it here.",
